course: dictionary
lesson: 13533
title: Tools and actions: the word implement
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An implement is a tool you use to do a job. «Grandad used a garden implement to dig up the weeds.» A spade, a rake and a trowel are all garden implements. A pencil, pen or crayon is a writing implement.
explain: Implement can also be a verb, which means to put a plan or rule into action. «The school will implement a new reading rule next term.» The school is not buying a tool here. It is making the rule happen. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is it something people do?
explain: Look at the words around implement to find its meaning. Tools, jobs and garden words suggest a thing. Plans, rules and governments suggest doing something. The context tells you which sense you need.
fact: An implement is a tool or instrument for doing a particular job.
fact: As a verb, «implement» means to put a plan, rule or idea into action.
fact: «Implements» can mean tools in history, like «Stone Age implements made of flint».
fact: In computing, «implement» means writing the code that makes something work.
exercise: «Grandad used a garden implement to dig up the weeds.» What is a garden implement? | A kind of bird | A fence around the garden | *A tool for a job in the garden | A plant that grows in the garden
exercise: «The council will implement the new plan in June.» What does implement mean here? | Argue about the plan with friends | Write a poem about the plan | Forget the plan | *Put the plan into action
exercise: «Stone Age people made sharp implements from flint.» Find and copy the word that means tools. | *implements | flint | Stone Age | sharp
test: «Pack a writing implement for the test.» What is a writing implement? | A kind of paper bag | A book of stories | *A pencil or pen, a tool for writing | A pair of shoes
test: «The school will implement a healthier lunch rule.» What does implement mean in this sentence? | *Put into action | Give up on | Tell a joke about | Measure
exam: Which sentence uses implement to mean put into action? | The spade is an old garden implement. | *The head teacher will implement the new homework rule. | The farmer oiled his implement. | Ella bought a new writing implement.
